# Command Module Pattern

- Export `{ match(text, lcText, deps), execute(matchResult, deps) }`.
- `match` returns parsed data (truthy) or `null`. Never throw from `match`.
- Admin-only: `if (deps.ima !== 'admin') return null;` FIRST line of `match`.
- `deps` = `{ context, member, email, ima, db, redis, usersCollection, execFileAsync, bot }` — destructure only what you use.
- Reply via `context.sendActivity(MessageFactory.text(...))` from `botbuilder`.
- Card-submit handlers read `context.activity.value.msteams.type` (see `server/commands/ticketSubmit.js`).
- Update edits: `context.updateActivity({ type: 'message', id: context.activity.value.activityId, conversation: context.activity.conversation, ... })`.
- Register the module in the `commands` array in `server/commands/index.js`. Order matters — first match wins.
- Add a `match()` test in `test/commands.test.js`.
- HTTP via `axios`. Form posts: `new URLSearchParams(params)` + `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded`.
- DB via `deps.db.query(sql, params)` with `?`/`??` placeholders (mysql2 promise pool).
- Redis via `deps.redis.get`/`set`/`sadd`/`srem`/`smembers`.
- Multi-action commands use `{ action: '...', ...payload }` + `switch` in `execute` (see `githubIssues.js`).
